// Tool-neutral MCP server catalog.
//
// Add your real MCP servers here, one entry per server, keyed by server
// name. Setup steps for each tool (Claude Code, Codex CLI) read this file
// and render it into that tool's native MCP config format/container.
//
// Keep commands portable: use `$HOME` and `$REPO` placeholders instead of
// absolute paths so this file works across machines and checkouts. `$REPO`
// is substituted with this repo's absolute path at bootstrap time; `$HOME`
// is resolved by the shell/tool at launch time.
//
// SECURITY: this file is PUBLIC (deny-list + secret scanner gate pushes).
// Only put shareable servers here -- use $HOME/$REPO placeholders and
// `${ENV_VAR}` interpolation for tokens; never inline secrets or internal
// hostnames. Personal/secret servers belong in a LOCAL, non-repo file that
// pi-mcp-adapter also reads (e.g. ~/.config/mcp/mcp.json), not here.
//
// The entry below is a disabled placeholder example -- `"disabled": true`
// stops the adapter from trying to connect. Replace or remove it and add
// your own shareable servers.
{
  "example-server": {
    "command": "npx",
    "args": ["-y", "@scope/mcp-server"],
    "env": {},
    "disabled": true
  }
}
